Title: Restore 32-bit Windows builds in vcbuild.bat
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

Node refuses x86 before it does anything else:

  "32-bit Windows builds are not supported anymore."

That is a policy gate, not a removal. Everything behind it still works --
vcbuild.bat still maps both `ia32` and `x86` onto target_arch=x86, still passes
--dest-cpu=x86 to configure, still finds nasm for it and still builds the right
vcvarsall argument; configure.py still lists `ia32` in valid_arch. What was
lost with the gate is two lines that used to go with it, and both are needed
before an x86 build reaches the end.

--no-cross-compiling. configure.py decides `cross_compiling` as
`target_arch != host_arch`, so ia32 against an x64 host counts as a cross
build and sets want_separate_host_toolset, which makes GYP emit a *_host
project beside every target one. GYP's msvs generator cannot express that: the
host projects get no configuration matching the solution's, and the build
stops with one of these per project --

  error MSB8013: This project doesn't contain the Configuration and Platform
  combination of Release|x64. [.../simdutf_host.vcxproj]

It is also not really a cross build. A 32-bit torque or mksnapshot runs
perfectly well on 64-bit Windows under WoW64, which is how 32-bit Node was
built here for years. --no-cross-compiling is configure.py's own override for
exactly this, and it sets want_separate_host_toolset back to 0.

The gate's condition was already the right one; it just bailed instead of
doing the thing x86 needs, so it is reused rather than deleted.

msbplatform. The line mapping x86 to an MSBuild platform went with the gate,
leaving x64 as the default and arm64 as the only override -- so an x86 build
generated a Win32 solution and then asked MSBuild for a configuration it does
not have:

  node.sln.metaproj : error MSB4126: The specified solution configuration
  "Release|x64" is invalid.

Win32 rather than x86 because that is GYP's name for it: msvs.py defaults
msvs_configuration_platform to "Win32" and the solution it writes says Win32
throughout. The two spellings are not interchangeable at this layer.

The same restoration Electron needed. Upstream dropped win32-ia32 in #51816
and patches/other/07-restore-32-bit.patch puts it back there; this is that
change for Node's own build.

Not covered here: the MSI. tools/msvs/msi/nodemsi.sln carries only x64 and
ARM64 configurations and nodemsi.wixproj defaults Platform to x64, so
`vcbuild msi` on x86 fails the same way for the same reason. Building node.exe
does not go near it.

Note for anyone regenerating this: vcbuild.bat is CRLF throughout and the
hunks have to keep it. A patch that converts these lines to LF applies and
leaves a file cmd.exe parses differently.

diff --git a/vcbuild.bat b/vcbuild.bat
--- a/vcbuild.bat
+++ b/vcbuild.bat
@@ -252,10 +252,7 @@
 if defined cfg              set configure_flags=%configure_flags% --control-flow-guard
 if defined v8windbg         set configure_flags=%configure_flags% --enable-v8windbg
 
-if "%target_arch%"=="x86" (
-  echo "32-bit Windows builds are not supported anymore."
-  exit /b 1
-)
+if "%target_arch%"=="x86" set configure_flags=%configure_flags% --no-cross-compiling
 
 if not exist "%~dp0deps\icu" goto no-depsicu
 if "%target%"=="Clean" echo deleting %~dp0deps\icu
@@ -434,6 +431,7 @@
 set "msbcpu=/m:2"
 if "%NUMBER_OF_PROCESSORS%"=="1" set "msbcpu=/m:1"
 set "msbplatform=x64"
+if "%target_arch%"=="x86" set "msbplatform=Win32"
 if "%target_arch%"=="arm64" set "msbplatform=ARM64"
 if "%target%"=="Build" (
   if defined no_cctest set target=node
